lines=['# Track A — Resource-First Preflight','','**TRACK_A_READY_FOR_ARCHITECTURAL_FREEZE_REVIEW** — proposal only. No prototype or new registry object exists. Three explicit shared capability gaps have bounded proposals for review; implementation is blocked until architectural approval. No unresolved external source is required to review this package.','','Current authority: `WAVE_2_CURRENT_AUTHORITY.json`, user Track A attachment and accepted W2-C01/C02/C03/C06. Existing GR01–06 freeze inputs and literal registry statuses remain unchanged. This scope authorizes specification only; no GR numbering, Track B, PM stress or HRBA reconstruction is inferred.','','## Governing design learning','','GR06 architecture works, but user review identifies excessive density/length: nested stages/tabs, prompts, selections and repeated authored responses. Treat it as the upper end of authored-work burden, not a production course-screen template. Track A replaces it with four supplied artifacts, three criterion rows, two short fields and one current-version reconsideration. No production changes to GR06 follow from this observation.','','## Resource dispositions','','| ID | Resource | Disposition | Decision and limit |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |']+[f"| {r['id']} | {r['title']} | {r['disposition']} | {r['reason']} |" for r in resources]+['','Every inspected file, byte size, source scope and SHA-256 is recorded in `TRACK_A_RESOURCE_INVENTORY_v0.1.json`. External trees remain read-only. No entire external application was rerun or independently recertified; old HRBA/PM screens and visuals do not override current system authority.','', '## Selection and System Gap decisions','','Use the existing shell/control/state foundation; harvest the PM answer-neutral gate and immutable version/traceability patterns. Propose `BLK-ASSESSMENT-BUNDLE-01`, `INT-READINESS-REVIEW-01`, `IP-READINESS-GATE-01`, all PROPOSED_NOT_REGISTERED. Propose `readiness-review` variants of CMP-EVIDENCE-DECISION-01 and TPL-SCENARIO-01, likewise unregistered. No existing manifest is broadened in this task. TPL-SCENARIO currently supports only INT-JUDGMENT; compatibility is a legitimate TA-G03 gap to approve and test centrally.','','TA-G01 owns versioned artifact/criterion representation; TA-G02 owns assessment/reconsideration/staleness; TA-G03 owns compact arrangement compatibility. SVC-LEARNING-STATE remains unchanged and cannot grant readiness, authorization or credentials. Do not copy the deep workspace just because it saves drafts.','','## Coverage and next boundary','','This proposed composite covers integrated capability-evidence review, readiness judgment, feedback/remediation, reconsideration, honest practice completion and the required accessibility/resilience baseline. It does not close actual independent competence assessment, credentials, live Hub transfer, portfolio return, peer exchange, co-creation or Gate-8 final equivalence. Those remain separately governed capabilities. Track A is a capability label, not an invented GR-07 assignment.','','Deliverables: deterministic design, exact JSON contract proposal, canonical differentiation brief (Markdown and JSON), planned V01–V22 matrix, semantic fixtures and source notes. Current checks verify documents, references, schemas, preservation and package only. No future prototype/manual test is reported PASS.']
(OUT/'TRACK_A_RESOURCE_FIRST_PREFLIGHT_v0.1.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
notes='''# Track A — Research and Source Notes

Sources were consulted for this specification, not to certify the effectiveness of the proposed experience. Local inventory hashes identify the actual selected files; historical acceptance is distinguished from current build authority. External source paths are read-only provenance and will not be runtime dependencies.

## Research already cited in the repository

The existing GR06 research notes were inspected. The [CDC Step 5 guidance](https://www.cdc.gov/evaluation/php/evaluation-framework-action-guide/step-5-generate-and-support-conclusions.html), dated 2024-08-18, was successfully reopened in this task. It connects conclusions to agreed evidence expectations and asks that recommendations be feasible and contextual. **Design inference:** make criterion expectations, evidence links, limitations and a proportionate next step visible together. This is program-evaluation guidance applied by analogy, not empirical validation of capability assessment or this UI.

The existing repository notes report [Wylie, Koedinger and Mitamura (2009)](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~rwylie/papers/CogSci-2009-wylie_koedinger_mitamura.pdf) as a caution about indiscriminate self-explanation in a grammar tutoring context. Reopening the primary PDF timed out in this task; no new full-paper inspection or stronger research claim is made. The low-writing requirement comes directly from the user's GR06 review, not from extrapolating that study to HRBA. The earlier notes' OHCHR extract/full-text access limitation is preserved; it is not used to assert compliance or a new authoritative assessment rule.

No claim is made that three criteria, 80 words or an 8–12 minute target are validated learning-effect thresholds. They are explicit design proposals for human review and later observation. No new research library is required for freeze; assessment validity must be judged against the exact case and rubric.

## Local authority and source reconciliation

- HRBA final assessment explicitly uses ten objective questions, 80% scoring and retakes. Harvest domain coverage and remediation clarity; reject that scoring/certificate mechanism as Track A readiness authority. The supplied synthetic dossier is not the prior assessment, an actual student's portfolio or a real plan.
- HRBA module2 portfolio fields retain source-screen provenance. Harvest the identity connection, not its implementation or personal content. No production portfolio integration is claimed.
- PM identification-gate execution notes describe an answer-neutral gate and explicit consequence/confirmation/handoff. This is the strongest relevant rhythm. PM planning-gate historical notes prescribe a correct dependency/answer; the inspected current wrapper resolves instead to `FinalModule3Plan.tsx`. Those sources are not silently treated as identical or current visual authority. Harvest dependency/readiness and invalidation principles; reject preferred-option gates for Track A.
- PM implementation review connects status, quality and spending evidence but uses expected selections. Harvest cross-evidence scrutiny and safe follow-up; reject importing its current answers or visual system. PM closure readiness supplies a concise area/status representation, not a generic credential engine.
- The inspected Hub report distinguishes failed attempts, progress and certificate eligibility. That reinforces keeping practice records separate from actual authorization. A local text export is not a verified Hub receipt or a live portfolio workflow. The inspected Hub product/template specifications are reference context only.
- Mighty content-row and reveal-table images were visually inspected. The former supports calm criterion scanning; the latter contributes inline reveal mechanics only. No screenshot is claimed to be executable code; the horizontal table and bright vendor styling are not adopted.
- Current shared manifests reveal a genuine ownership gap: GR06 ledger functions expect source notes/interpretations/decision; scenario compatibility names only the judgment interaction. New assessment semantics therefore require explicit proposed shared owners and reviewed opt-in variants, not hidden reference-local adaptations.

## Semantic/provenance boundary

All TA-E01–E04 and TA-U01 wording is newly proposed synthetic learning content, explicitly grounded in existing fictional HRBA participation/response themes. It is not copied evidence of real events, not a strengthened replacement for the previously reviewed GR05/06 fixtures, and not an approved real-world plan. The exact proposed text is in the contract and review design. Separate semantic fixtures demonstrate possible reasoning; they are not learner-visible prepared answers.

GR06 H01–H09 remains ChatGPT-reviewed PASS, as reported by the user. Native Chrome 200% is now user-attested PASS; no performer/date/device detail beyond the supplied statement is invented. Actual screen-reader and physical-mobile software-keyboard checks remain pending. The user also identifies the writing/density burden as a design lesson, not a reversal of the recorded semantic pass.
'''
(OUT/'TRACK_A_RESEARCH_AND_SOURCE_NOTES_v0.1.md').write_text(notes,encoding='utf-8')
